mes the corresponding source paragraphs and its explanations narrate the accepted route, including the arbitrary-lattice coordinate-module/rank-one argument rather than a standard-lattice replacement. However, only T001 has a nontrivial-looking proposition, and it is merely ∀ i, True; T002 is also True-valued and T003–T007 are True. They export none of the formulas, lattice facts, conversion results, or witness facts described in their explanations. T008 states a terminal theorem but its internal premises are not meaningful established results. This is not a complete typed implementation of the source route.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument\"},{\"document\":\"source-map.json\",\"pointer\":\"/direct_boundaries/R001\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/statement\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/1/statement\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/2/statement\"}]},\"parameters_and_allowed_inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The surface binders include K with Field K, p : ℕ, lam : ℤ, M with additive/module instances, and D; the explicit hypotheses include primality, CharP K p, and 0 ≤ lam ∧ lam < p, matching source parameter ranges and preserving p=2 and lam=0. But H004 is not a faithful encoding of the original hypothesis: its actual predicate contains the conjunct LieIrreducible ℂ D.V D.x D.y D.z. That is a substantial irreducibility conclusion on the characteristic-zero module, absent from source H004 and not available as a source input. The structure additionally carries basis, embedding, operators and restrictions whose exact compatibility must not be mistaken for permission to assume the added irreducibility. Thus the proposed theorem may rely on a stronger hidden assumption even though direct-input IDs appear correct.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"spec.json\",\"pointer\":\"/hypotheses/3\"},{\"document\":\"source-context.md\",\"pointer\":\"/42-45\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/header\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/premises/3/type\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/32\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/inputs\"}]},\"representations_and_conversion_obligations\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"A free ℤ-module M with a basis and an injective embedding can model an arbitrary lattice; this is not itself a standard-basis substitution. However, the source output and S004 use M ⊗[ℤ] K, while the actual contract conclusion and terminal plan type use K ⊗[ℤ] M. The representation notes acknowledge TensorProduct.comm as a necessary conversion, but neither the contract nor plan provides a typed bridge theorem, its operator-compatibility obligations, or an assembly step consuming it. These presentations are not definitionally identical, and merely recording a canonical commutor does not prove or apply the required equivalence. In addition, D.H004's hidden characteristic-zero irreducibility is an unallowed representation assumption, not a conversion obligation.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion/type\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/header\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation_notes\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/7\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/4\"}]},\"statements_and_local_plans\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The full elaborated signatures show T001 : ∀ i : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), True, and T002 : ∀ i j, True; T003–T007 have type True. Thus the source claims described in the explanations are not the conclusions of those obligations, and their later uses cannot convey any S001–S007 facts. T008's complete type concludes LieIrreducible on K ⊗[ℤ] M, not the source-facing M ⊗[ℤ] K output, and there is no plan obligation to transport it back. Moreover its H004 premise supplies characteristic-zero LieIrreducibility directly. The type-check receipt establishes elaboration of these signatures only; it does not certify semantic fidelity or completed proof bodies.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/premises/3/type\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion/type\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/7/statement\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/37-44\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"}]}},\"findings\":[{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"explanation\":\"H004 is materially stronger than source H004: the actual expanded predicate ends with LieIrreducible ℂ D.V D.x D.y D.z. This assumes characteristic-zero irreducibility rather than proving the source derivation from the stated highest-weight and lattice hypotheses.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"spec.json\",\"pointer\":\"/hypotheses/3\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/header\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/21-32\"}]},{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"explanation\":\"The terminal contract/plan target is on K ⊗[ℤ] M, whereas source P is on M ⊗[ℤ] K. The notes mention the tensor commutor but no typed conversion/transport obligation is in the plan; the source-facing target is therefore not established.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion/type\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation_notes\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/7\"}]},{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"explanation\":\"The local propositions T001–T007 are placeholders (True or universally quantified True) rather than the basis/action, matrix-unit, arbitrary-lattice, scalar-extension, or invariant-subspace conclusions claimed in their explanations. Consequently this typed plan does not encode or discharge the source inference, regardless of whether the placeholders could be proved.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/1\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/2\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/3\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/4\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/5\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/6\"}]}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and accep